spu_coh_bitmap.h: g_spu_coh_bits as __declspec(selectany) on MinGW too, not __attribute__((weak)).

Symptom: ps3recomp v0.18.0 (4e8f3ca) does not link kz2.exe: "undefined reference to
`g_spu_coh_bits'" from main.cpp.obj (.refptr.g_spu_coh_bits) and ppu_loader.cpp.obj (spu_coh_line_reserved). Cause:
upstream #534 defines the PPU-store bitmap pointer in the header, selectany under MSVC and weak elsewhere. On a PE
target GCC's weak definition is a weak external with a per-object default, and MinGW ld (binutils 2.46) leaves it
undefined when C++ objects reach it through the .refptr indirection; reproduced with three objects (one C TU that
stores the pointer, two C++ TUs that read it): weak -> the same undefined references, selectany -> links. Fix: the
MSVC branch (selectany, a COMDAT "any": one definition kept, every object sees the same variable) also for
__MINGW32__; other toolchains unchanged. Upstream candidate (general: any MinGW build of v0.18.0).
Verification: the three-object repro under Proton prints "0 1 1" (not reserved before the store, reserved after,
one shared pointer); kz2.exe links.

diff --git a/runtime/spu/spu_coh_bitmap.h b/runtime/spu/spu_coh_bitmap.h
index 79bffe7..a8a61a8 100644
--- a/runtime/spu/spu_coh_bitmap.h
+++ b/runtime/spu/spu_coh_bitmap.h
@@ -17,7 +17,10 @@
 
 #include <stdint.h>
 
-#if defined(_MSC_VER)
+#if defined(_MSC_VER) || defined(__MINGW32__)
+/* KZ2 patch 6033: selectany on MinGW too. GCC's weak definition on a PE target is a weak external with a
+ * per-object default; with the C++ objects' .refptr indirection, MinGW ld left g_spu_coh_bits undefined in
+ * kz2.exe's link (ppu_loader.cpp, main.cpp). selectany (a COMDAT "any") is what the MSVC branch already uses. */
 #  define SPU_COH_SHARED __declspec(selectany)
 #else
 #  define SPU_COH_SHARED __attribute__((weak))
